ing n-butyl-2-cyanoacrylate for gastric variceal bleeding</article-title><source>J Gastroenterol Hepatol</source><year>1999</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>250</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10197494</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snady</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role of sclerotherapy in the treatment of esophageal varices: personal experience and a review of randomized trials</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>1987</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>813</fpage><lpage>822</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3115089</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Korula</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ko</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Demonstration of two distinct subsets of gastric varices. Observations during a seven-year study of endoscopic sclerotherapy</article-title><source>Dig Dis Sci</source><year>1991</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>309</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1995266</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Foda</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An unusual complication of histoacryl injection</article-title><source>Endoscopy</source><year>1997</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>140</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9101163</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label>